#+TITLE: Cador rejects ssget crossing mode _C required by SCHMS occupancy tests
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: compatibility
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-29

* Reproduction and scope

SCHMS+ branch =fix-pb-lisp-warnings= adds three native ActiveX regression
scenarios for =src-vlx/encombrement.lsp=,
=schms_chevauchement_encombrement_sauf=. They select actual drawing entities
with =ssget "_C"=, check exclusion of VLA objects and preservation of the
caller's =ename= binding. No CAD primitive is mocked.

The tests cannot execute this operation under clautolisp SBCL 2.3.73,
=--host cador --dialect bricscad-v26=. The installed Windows release 2.3.75
has the same selection dispatcher; current master 7411ff07 still rejects
all modes except X/_X/_I in =clautolisp/cador/source/selection-api.lisp=.
This is a missing host capability, not a regression attributed to a release.

Run the adjacent =ssget-crossing-selection-unsupported-repro.lsp= with:

#+begin_src sh
clautolisp --no-init --host cador --dialect bricscad-v26 \
  -l issues/open/ssget-crossing-selection-unsupported-repro.lsp
#+end_src

Observed error:

#+begin_example
cador does not yet support ssget mode "_C"; accepted modes are "X", "_X" and "_I".
#+end_example

The fixture contains exactly two lines inside the crossing rectangle. A
supported implementation must return a selection containing both entities;
this reproducer prints PASS only after testing length and membership. It
cleans its own two entities on success and on the caught unsupported-mode
error. It needs no SCHMS installation or external DWG.

* Expected implementation and checks

Implement crossing selection with geometric intersection, including entities
crossing a boundary with neither endpoint inside; do not approximate it by
selecting all drawing entities. Test fully inside, crossing, outside, boundary,
empty selection, filters, and supported dialect/coordinate conventions.
Compare these semantics against native AutoCAD and BricsCAD before claiming
parity, especially view-dependent behaviour and UCS/WCS conversion.

SCHMS currently activates these three scenarios only in the actual native
CAD launchers, including the optimized DES/VLX qualification. Its existing
11 ActiveX tests still run in Cador; the output explicitly states the three
additional cases are outside that backend's current coverage. Once _C is
implemented, enable the same cases in the Cador lane and keep this minimal
reproducer in the implementation regression suite.
